SF Symbols artwork
==================

The PNG files in this directory are SF Symbols, drawn by macOS through AppKit and
recoloured and resized by tools/sf_symbols.swift. Apple publishes no artwork files and no
licence file to copy alongside them, so this notice records the terms instead.

SF Symbols are system-provided images under the Xcode and Apple SDKs Agreement. Section
2.11 of that agreement licenses them for use in developing applications for Apple-branded
products, which is what this repository is part of. They are not redistributable for any
other purpose: anyone reusing this gem outside that context should show the SF Symbols
names alone and leave these files behind.

Apple's published guidance for the set also asks that the symbols, and glyphs
substantially or confusingly similar to them, are not used in app icons, logos, or any
other trademark-related use, and that certain symbols standing for Apple features and
products are used only to refer to those features and products. Nothing here is drawn on
an icon or a logo. One symbol in the set names an Apple feature — `touchid`, which the
`:fingerprint` concept uses — and on an Apple platform, where these names are the only
ones drawn, that is the feature it refers to. The generic `smartphone` is used for
`:mobile` in preference to `iphone` for the same reason.

Reference: https://developer.apple.com/sf-symbols/
